window.DRUK_I18N = { en: {"lang":"en","meta":"Druk Voyages - Kingdom of Bhutan Travel","description":"Druk Voyages - Bhutan's trusted travel agency. Curated itineraries, festival journeys, trekking, and wellness retreats in the Kingdom of Happiness.","tagline":"Authentic Bhutan, Extraordinary Journeys","heroMottos":["A little closer<br> to <em>wonder.</em>","Where mountains<br> meet <em>meaning.</em>","Ancient stories.<br> Living <em>traditions.</em>","Take the path<br> less <em>hurried.</em>","A kingdom that<br> stays <em>with you.</em>","Walk where<br> prayers <em>fly.</em>"],"heroDescriptions":["Quiet valleys. Living traditions. Extraordinary people. Discover Bhutan through journeys shaped by the locals who call it home.","Follow forest trails to cliffside monasteries and open Himalayan horizons. In Bhutan, the journey invites you to pause, look closer, and breathe.","Step into dzong courtyards, discover the artistry of sacred festivals, and meet the craftspeople who keep Bhutan’s heritage alive.","Wander through peaceful valleys, share a farmhouse meal, and leave room for unexpected moments. Discover Bhutan at a pace that feels like your own.","From prayer flags on mountain passes to warm welcomes in village homes, find the moments that turn a Bhutan journey into a lasting memory."],"gnhPillars":["Sustainable &amp; Equitable<br>Socio-Economic Development","Conservation of<br>Environment","Preservation &amp; Promotion<br>of Culture","Good<br>Governance"],"menu":["About","Itineraries","Experiences","Gallery","Plan My Trip"],"hero":["Bhutan, beyond the ordinary","A little closer<br>to <em>wonder.</em>","Quiet valleys. Living traditions. Extraordinary people. Discover Bhutan through journeys shaped by the locals who call it home.","Explore Journeys","Meet Your Local Guides","Scroll"],"stats":["Years in Bhutan","Guests Welcomed","Curated Itineraries","Satisfaction Rate"],"marquee":["Tiger's Nest Monastery","Paro Tsechu Festival","Punakha Dzong","Black-Necked Cranes","Dochula Pass","Bumthang Valley","Rhododendron Blooms","Meditation Retreats"],"about":["Gross National<br>Happiness","Who We Are","Bhutan's Most <em>Trusted</em> Journey Architects","Druk Voyages was founded by Bhutanese locals who believe genuine travel transforms both visitor and visited. We are one of the few agencies fully owned and operated within the Kingdom - every dollar spent directly uplifts local communities.","The Bhutanese government's Sustainable Development Fee funds free healthcare and education for every citizen. With us, you are not just a tourist - you are a guardian of this living heritage.","Licensed by the Tourism Council of Bhutan","Carbon-neutral operations since 2018","100% locally owned & staffed","Bespoke small-group experiences"],"aboutMore":["Bhutan is not a place you tick off a list. It is a kingdom you are welcomed into — and for more than fifteen years we have made sure that welcome feels personal.","Guided by those who call it home","Your guides are licensed Bhutanese who call these valleys home. They know when the monastery bells ring at dawn, which farmhouse kitchen welcomes guests, and when it is time simply to stop and listen.","Shaped around you","No fixed departures and no crowded coaches. Your route, pace and stays are designed around what moves you, from front-row festival days to silent forest retreats.","Travel that gives back","We are locally owned and staffed, and carbon-neutral since 2018, so what you spend stays in Bhutanese hands and the mountains stay as clear as you found them.","Begin your journey with us"],"aboutGnh":["Why Gross National Happiness","The kingdom’s compass, and ours","Bhutan measures its progress by Gross National Happiness rather than by economic growth alone. Its four pillars below shape how the kingdom welcomes visitors — high value, low volume — and they shape every journey we plan: respectful of culture, gentle on the land, and good for the communities you meet."],"journeys":["Journeys with a sense of place","Your next chapter,<br><em>somewhere extraordinary.</em>","All journeys","Culture","Festivals","Trekking","Wellness"],"gallery":["A glimpse of the kingdom","A place like <em>no other.</em>","A few of the moments waiting for you: quiet courtyards, mountain air, living traditions, and a different kind of everyday."],"experience":["Signature Moments","Experiences That <em>Stay Forever</em>",["Tiger's Nest Pilgrimage","A 4-hour guided ascent to Paro Taktsang, where Guru Rinpoche meditated for 3 months, perched 900m above the valley floor on sheer cliffs."],["Dzong Architecture Tours","Private after-hours access to Punakha Dzong - the Palace of Great Happiness - where monks still practice 17th-century rituals at dusk."],["Tsechu Festival Immersion","Witness masked Cham dances performed only during sacred festivals. Front-row viewing and authentic cultural exchange with local families."],["Farm-to-Table Farming Life","Spend dawn to dusk with a Phobjikha Valley farmer - planting red rice, milking yaks, and learning the art of ema datshi."],["Himalayan Wellness Retreat","Three-day silent retreat with traditional Sowa Rigpa medicine, hot stone baths, and meditation guided by a certified Buddhist master."],["Black-Necked Crane Safari","Every November, endangered cranes migrate to Phobjikha Valley. Dawn wildlife watches in pristine wetlands with ornithologist guides."]],"planning":["Travel Planning","Best Time to <em>Visit Bhutan</em>","Bhutan is magical year-round but each season unlocks a completely different kingdom.",["Spring","March - May","Rhododendrons explode in colour. Clear skies reveal Himalayan peaks. Paro Tsechu festival draws thousands."],["Monsoon","June - August","Lush emerald valleys, minimal crowds, lower rates. Rain makes forests and waterfalls spectacular."],["Autumn","Sep - November","Crystal-clear Himalayan views, golden valleys, and the spectacular Thimphu Tsechu. Peak season."],["Winter","Dec - February","Snow-dusted dzongs, black-necked crane season, crisp air for lower altitude treks. Deeply peaceful."]],"enquiry":["Start Planning","Tell Us Your<br><em>Dream Journey</em>","Every Bhutan journey is unique. Our travel architects will craft a bespoke itinerary based on your interests, travel dates, and group size - at no obligation.","Mon-Sat - 9am-6pm Bhutan Time","First Name *","Last Name *","Email *","Phone","Interested In","Number of Guests","Planned Arrival","Duration (Days)","Your Dream Journey *","Select a journey type...",["Classic Highlights","Festival Journey","Himalayan Trekking","Wellness Retreat","Photography Tour","Honeymoon Package","Custom / Other"],"Tell us about your travel style, interests, and any special requirements...","Send Enquiry"],"testimonials":["Guest Stories","Words From Our <em>Travellers</em>","Druk Voyages curated every moment with extraordinary care. Standing at Tiger's Nest at sunrise with no other visitors was the most spiritual experience of my life.","The festival immersion was beyond anything I imagined. Our guide arranged a private dinner with a monk who taught us about Buddhist philosophy over butter tea. Transformative.","The wellness retreat completely reset my mind. The hot stone bath under the stars in Bumthang Valley - I still think about it every single day.","New York, USA - Autumn 2025","London, UK - Spring 2025","Tokyo, Japan - Winter 2025"],"cta":["Begin Your Journey","Ready to Enter the Last <em>Shangri-La?</em>","Every journey to Bhutan is unique. Tell us your dream and our Bhutanese travel architects will design the perfect itinerary - exclusively for you.","Plan My Trip","Call Thimphu Office"],"footer":["Licensed by the Tourism Council of Bhutan. 100% Bhutanese-owned, committed to sustainable travel that protects the Kingdom's living heritage.","Itineraries","Destinations","Contact",["Classic Highlights","Festival Journeys","Himalayan Trekking","Wellness Retreats","Photography Tours","Honeymoon Packages"],"Mon-Sat 9am-6pm","© 2026 Druk Voyages. All rights reserved. Tourism Council of Bhutan Lic. #TCB-2009-142.","Privacy","Terms","Sitemap"],"ui":{"language":"Language","menu":"Menu","view":"View Itinerary","from":"From","perPerson":"per person","close":"Close Itinerary","dayByDay":"Day-by-Day Itinerary","pp":"pp","days":"Days","max":"Max","couple":"Couple Only","difficulties":{"Easy":"Easy","Moderate":"Moderate","Challenging":"Challenging"},"required":"Please fill in all required fields.","sending":"Sending...","success":"Thank you! Our team will be in touch within 24 hours.","toast":"Enquiry sent successfully!","fail":"Could not send your enquiry. Please email us directly at hello@drukvoyages.bt","slide":"Slide"},"itineraries":[]} };
